{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-14T11:35:19.613Z","data":{"text":"I've completed the task. Summary of what I did:\n\n**Implementation**\n- **New `src/core/status/inbox-paused.ts`**: exports `PausedItem` and `projectPaused(overview, nowMs)`, which reads each approved active change's `readActivePause` and builds `{ change, task, pausedUntil, command: \"osq show <id>\" }` when the pause names one of its tasks.\n- **`src/core/status/inbox.ts`**: `Inbox.running` becomes `(RunningItem | PausedItem)[]` plus the one type import (file stays at 249 lines; `projectRunning` unchanged).\n- **`src/core/status/inbox-projection.ts`**: `readInbox` merges the paused items into `running`, drops a paused task that also has a live running item, and sorts by numeric change then task.\n- **`src/core/status/inbox-text.ts`**: renders paused rows as `  <id>: <title> — task <n>: <title> — paused until <time> — osq show <id>` via `formatPauseUntil`.\n- **`packages/ui/src/home/RunningGroup.tsx`**: paused items show `paused until <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM> UTC` in place of elapsed, formatted in-component.\n- New `tests/usage-pause-inbox.test.ts` and `tests/ui-home-paused.test.tsx`.\n\n**Verification**: the task verify passes (4 tests), and so does `pnpm verify` (typechecks, build, all 215+ tests, lint).\n\n**Deviation** (documented in the result file): because the out-of-scope preexisting `tests/inbox.test.ts` reads `.pid`/`.startedAt`/`.elapsedSeconds` directly off `Inbox['running'][number]`, `PausedItem` declares those live-only fields as `never` (cast at construction). Runtime objects still carry exactly `change`, `task`, `pausedUntil`, `command`, so the JSON contract holds; the `never` members only keep the union element's live-field access legally typed. The task should have set `tests.modify`/scope for `tests/inbox.test.ts` to avoid this."}}
